**Most notable finding:** The benchmark surfaced a genuine PRD self-contradiction in §3.8 — the close operation was specified as *both* rejecting open assignments (`ERR_OPEN_ASSIGNMENTS`) *and* force-clearing them via a safety cascade (mutually exclusive). The implementation adopted precondition-wins; Step 7 deleted the one non-derivable test, and Steps 8/9 pinned the PRD prose to match. Step 9 additionally closed several silences the implementation resolved at generation time (logical-clock timestamps, server-wide monotonic incident-number counter, recommendation null-pool semantics, field-pipeline role/token rules, metrics-computed-once-and-stored).

All durable artifacts (scaffold, design indices, PRD variants, tests, implementation, `results.{1..8}.json`, and a complete per-step `worklog.md`) are persisted under `tasks/task_0488_cad_911_dispatch/`.
